of the genetically obese Zucker rats</article-title><source>Eur J Pharmacol</source><year>1995</year><volume>293</volume><fpage>385</fpage><lpage>393</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8748692</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Weltman</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name><name><surname>Farrell</surname><given-names>GC</given-names></name><name><surname>Liddle</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Increased hepatocyte CYP2E1 expression in a rat nutritional model of hepatic steatosis with inflammation</article-title><source>Gastroenterology</source><year>1996</year><volume>111</volume><fpage>1645</fpage><lpage>1653</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8942745</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Corbett</surname><given-names>SW</given-names></name><name><surname>Stern</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Keesey</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Energy expenditure in rats with diet-induced obesity</article-title><source>Am J Clin Nutr</source><year>1986</year><volume>44</volume><fpage>173</fpage><lpage>180</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3728354</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Factors influencing energy intake of rats fed either a high-fat or a fat mimetic diet</article-title><source>Int J Obes Relat Metab Disord</source><year>1994</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>632</fpage><lpage>640</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7812418</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hill</surname><given-names>JO</given-names></name><nam